Rast <rast2@hotmail.com> wrote:
>What does this mean?  Does every weapon a kobold uses do d4 damage, or is 
>the d4 added to the normal damage of whatever weapon it happens to have?  
>Does it get a strength bonus?  What is the damage when it has no weapon? 

The force of the kobold's blow always does 1d4 damage.  If it is wielding
a weapon, the weapon's damage is added to that 1d4 - so a kobold with a
+3 silver saber will do (1d4 + 1d8 + 3) = 5-15 damage.

This is why attacking aligned priests is quite dangerous even if you do
have MR and shock resistance; one of their melee attacks is W4d10.
